The build flow may fetch, mount, or execute third-party components such as
Zephyr, MCUboot, Zephyr SDK toolchains, Arduino CLI, HPatchLite, and container
base images. Those components are provided by their respective projects and are
governed by their own licenses and notices. Keeping a Zephyr workspace in a
Docker or Podman volume does not change the ownership or licensing of those
upstream sources.

RAKWireless board names such as RAK4631, RAK3172, RAK11720, and RAK4200 refer
to the target hardware modules and boards. They do not imply that this package
is published by or officially supported by RAKWireless.
